WEBVTT

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.510
Meet Mags.

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.840
Mags collects shiny claims.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.500
She grabs the claim, and leaves the source behind.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.450
Months later, a customer orders at seven.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.930
The help page says too late.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.880
The newest note says eight.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.470
Knowledge puts the source back on the claim.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.150
Your agent reads the notes into a map.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.310
Every link keeps its quote, its source and its date.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.130
Ask when orders close.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.740
You get a timeline: six until May twentieth, then eight.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.190
The help page gets a flag.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.470
A possible contradiction, for you to decide.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:45.840
Ask something vague, and it asks you back.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.790
A link is a lead, not proof.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.740
Read the quote.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:04.710
Knowledge.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.400
Follow a claim back to the evidence.
